{
 "id": "MoonPhase",
 "name": "moon-phase",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Moon phase",
 "prompt": "Draw the moon at any phase of its cycle, from new through full and back, without glyphs or images; show the eight principal phases captioned, and one bound to a variable.",
 "level": 2,
 "use_cases": [
  "widget",
  "watch-face",
  "calendar"
 ],
 "form_factor": "phone",
 "keywords": [
  "moon",
  "moon phase",
  "lunar",
  "lunar phase",
  "crescent",
  "gibbous",
  "full moon",
  "new moon",
  "first quarter",
  "last quarter",
  "moon icon"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "{\"MoonPhase\": {\"phase\": 0.3}} draws a 48 dp moon; phase is the fraction of the lunation (0 new, 0.25 first quarter, 0.5 full, 0.75 last quarter) and may be a variable or an expression from the clock",
  "One definition draws every phase: a disc in the shade colour, the lit half (right while waxing, step(phase, 0.5) flips it), and a terminator ellipse of half-width r·|cos 2π·phase|, shaded for a crescent and lit for a gibbous moon",
  "Draw in a 100-unit box and scale it to size once; with a literal phase every expression folds to a number, so a static moon costs no expressions"
 ],
 "snippets": [
  {
   "pointer": "/root/column/children/1/row/children/0/column/children/0",
   "shows": "draw.transform",
   "note": "0, a new moon: the 100-unit drawing scaled to 48 dp, a rim and an unlit disc"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/column/children/1/row/children/1/column/children/0",
   "shows": "draw.arc",
   "note": "0.125, a waxing crescent: the right half lit, then a shaded ellipse over it"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/column/children/1/row/children/3/column/children/0",
   "shows": "draw.shapes",
   "note": "0.375, a waxing gibbous moon: the right half and a lit ellipse"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/root/column/children/3/row/children/0",
   "shows": "data.expression",
   "note": "bound to the exported variable phase: the terminator follows cos(2π·@phase)"
  }
 ],
 "inputs": {
  "variables": {
   "phase": {
    "type": "float",
    "meaning": "lunation fraction 0..1 of the large moon",
    "default": 0.3,
    "min": 0,
    "max": 1,
    "step": 0.01
   }
  },
  "clock": null,
  "touch": false
 },
 "check": {
  "describe": "Two rows of four 48 dp moons, captioned with the phase and its name: 0 new (an empty disc inside its rim), 0.125 a thin crescent lit on the right, 0.25 the right half lit, 0.375 gibbous lit on the right, 0.5 full, 0.625 gibbous lit on the left, 0.75 the left half lit, 0.875 a crescent on the left. Below, a 72 dp moon bound to phase 0.3 (a waxing gibbous moon, 65% lit). Dark: amber on slate; light: the theme's darker amber on pale grey; mono and mono inverted: the lit part in onSurface, the rest background inside a grey ring. At 260 dp the columns close up and at 480 dp they spread; the moons keep their size.",
